+---
+title: Regex-based ParamType parsing (click.Duration)
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-16
+cost: { minutes: 2, tokens: 49726 }
+touches:
+  - docs/api.md
+  - docs/parameter-types.md
+  - src/click/__init__.py
+  - src/click/types.py
+  - tests/test_types.py
+---
+
+## Decided
+- click.Duration (src/click/types.py) parses with one compiled regex using re.fullmatch and flags re.ASCII | re.IGNORECASE. A bare integer is seconds; otherwise ordered d/h/m/s groups. A (?=\d) lookahead keeps the empty string from matching the all-optional branch.
+- Only str and timedelta are accepted. Any other input (including an int default) fails with "{value!r} is not a valid duration.", as the spec requires.
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- re.IGNORECASE without re.ASCII: Unicode case folding makes "s" match "ſ" (U+017F) and "k" match the Kelvin sign, and \d matches non-ASCII digits like "١٢".
+- re.match with "$": "$" also matches before a trailing newline, so "1h\n" would be accepted. Use fullmatch.
+
+## Watch out
+- int() on a digit string over 4300 chars raises ValueError (Python 3.11+ limit), and timedelta raises OverflowError for huge values. Both must go through self.fail, or a raw traceback reaches the user.
